    "text": "By Eileen Vargas ,\n1 days ago Mountain View’s downtown dinner scene has a new place where the steak arrives raw, the grill is built into the table, and the most expensive cuts are very much the point. Yakiniku Ginza is now serving Japanese barbecue with A5 wagyu, Australian wagyu, seafood, vegetables and enough tabletop cooking to make every diner part chef and part fire marshal. Read full article",
